{"_id":"6a2ff4b92204ffbc59e5a57a","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"3N5N6qe8JVr0XGOFdn5-8","description":"# Series and DataFrame\n\nA Series is a one-dimensional labeled array, analogous to a single column in a spreadsheet. A DataFrame is a two-dimensional table of Series that share an index, analogous to a spreadsheet or SQL table. These two structures are the foundation of all Pandas operations.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.Series","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.Series.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb89"},{"type":"official","title":"pandas.DataFrame","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb8a"},{"type":"article","title":"Pandas Series","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/pandas/pandas_series.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb8b"},{"type":"article","title":"Pandas DataFrames","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/pandas/pandas_dataframes.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb8c"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:48:57.948Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/3N5N6qe8JVr0XGOFdn5-8.md"}